# Millbrook's square: the mayor, the guard at the gate and Pip, and the player's own tally of what
# is left to do (progress), which the others jump to as each task is done. The tasks are flags: sign_hung (the
# baker's sign), wheel_found (the miller's wheel), cat_found (Pip's cat); fair_ready once all three
# are done. fair_cat_seen is the game's: it sets it when the player reaches the windmill. When the
# mayor has called everyone (opening), the game plays the ending (Sequences/FairOpens) and sets
# fair_opened once it has played.

conversation mayor in village
if not met_mayor
  set met_mayor
  @ mayor worried: Ah, a visitor! You've come on the evening of the fair, and we are nowhere near ready.
  @ mayor: The baker's stall has no sign, the miller's cart has lost a wheel, and Pip has lost her cat.
  choice
  > I'll help.
    play mayor emote-yes
    @ mayor happy: Splendid! Ask around the square. Everyone here knows a little of everything.
    @ mayor: Walk up to anyone and press {Interact} to talk.
  > Is it really that bad?
    @ mayor: Worse. Without a sign nobody finds the bread, and without the cart there are no benches.
    @ mayor: So yes. I'd be glad of a hand.
  end
else
  if fair_opened
    @ mayor happy: Have you tried Marta's buns? Go on, the fair's open!
  else
    if fair_ready
      @ mayor happy: Everything's done? Then gather round the fountain, everyone!
      set opening
    else
      @ mayor: How are we getting on?
      jump progress
    end
  end
end

conversation progress
if sign_hung
  if wheel_found
    if cat_found
      @ you: The sign, the wheel and the cat. That's everything. I should tell the mayor.
      set fair_ready
    else
      jump left
    end
  else
    jump left
  end
else
  jump left
end

conversation left
if not sign_hung
  @ you: The baker still needs her sign.
end
if not wheel_found
  @ you: The miller's cart is still on three wheels.
end
if not cat_found
  @ you: And Pip still hasn't found her cat.
end

conversation guard in village
if has_sign
  @ guard: Mind how you go. And mind that sign: the baker's been asking after it all day.
else
  @ guard: Evening. Welcome to Millbrook.
  choice
  > Have you seen anything odd today?
    @ guard: Odd? A sign fell off the miller's cart this morning. I've been keeping it safe.
    @ guard happy: It's the baker's. You'd be doing her a kindness.
    @ you: I'll take it to her.
    set has_sign
    if asked_cat
      @ guard: And a grey cat ran past me toward the windmill, if that's any use.
    end
  > Out of my way.
    play guard emote-no
    @ guard stern: Mind your manners in Millbrook, visitor.
  end
end

conversation pip in village
if cat_found
  @ pip happy: Whiskers is home! Thank you, thank you!
else
  if fair_cat_seen
    @ pip: You saw her? Up by the windmill?
    sound meow
    play pip emote-yes
    @ pip happy: She always goes there when the sails turn. I'll fetch her right now!
    set cat_found
    jump progress
  else
    @ pip worried: Have you seen my cat? She's small and grey, and she was right here a moment ago.
    set asked_cat
    @ you: I'll keep an eye out for her.
  end
end
